window.OSAP_FT=window.OSAP_FT||{};window.OSAP_FT["29"]={"https://theconversation.com/women-behind-bars-are-giving-birth-in-shackles-and-handcuffs-its-legal-but-it-shouldnt-be-294952":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:16Z","sha":"33fb4ac21ca89d2c119ce6da2505339db4ce534c2f8fe3e9842f1e4485a4edc9","read":"https://theconversation.com/women-behind-bars-are-giving-birth-in-shackles-and-handcuffs-its-legal-but-it-shouldnt-be-294952","bytes":179965,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Women behind bars are giving birth in shackles and handcuffs. It’s legal – but it shouldn’t be","by":[{"n":"Tatiana Corrales","r":"Senior Research Fellow, Law and Justice Hub, Jumbunna Institute for Indigenous Education and Research, University of Technology Sydney"}],"pub":"2026-11-16T03:11:25Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["“I was handcuffed to a belt and my legs were shackled. Because I was classified as a serious violent offender, they [medical staff] had to try and ultrasound around this big frickin’ belly chain.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["Liliana* was approximately ",["ten weeks pregnant","https://link.springer.com/rwe/10.1007/978-3-032-05038-0_79-1"]," when she first entered Victoria’s maximum security women’s prison. She experienced her entire pregnancy and gave birth to her son, Noah, behind bars."]},{"k":"p","s":["Her experience is not ",["unique","https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/18/indigenous-woman-shackled-during-labour-childbirth-queensland-ntwnfb"],". In Victoria, and in other Australia states, imprisoned women are giving birth and recovering from birth while restrained to hospital ",["beds","https://link.springer.com/rwe/10.1007/978-3-032-05038-0_79-1"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["But the practice violates the basic human rights of pregnant women and puts their health at risk."]},{"k":"h","s":["Birth behind bars"]},{"k":"p","s":["We don’t know a lot about how many women give birth in prison, or what happens to them during and following childbirth. ",["My new research","https://link.springer.com/rwe/10.1007/978-3-032-05038-0_79-1"]," looked at these issues in Victoria."]},{"k":"p","s":["I interviewed 26 participants, including prison officers, prison program staff, lawyers, community-based service providers and women who had been pregnant or given birth in prison. I wanted to understand what services and supports are available during pregnancy and following birth."]},{"k":"p","s":["Participants described the use of “closeting chains”, where women are shackled to their beds by their ankles, with chains long enough to allow for movement."]},{"k":"p","s":["One participant described a woman being “shackled to the bottom of the bed and handcuffed. She was shackled with her legs splayed to be able to give birth, and she wasn’t able to have any dignity”."]},{"k":"p","s":["Prison officers are always present during childbirth. Sometimes they are inside the birthing suite, but they can also be stationed outside a woman’s room."]},{"k":"p","s":["In ",["my research","https://link.springer.com/rwe/10.1007/978-3-032-05038-0_79-1"],", the use of shackles during and following birth was justified on the basis that these women may pose a risk to themselves or other people."]},{"k":"p","s":["One of the most common reasons provided was that women may try to escape from the hospital. This was a particular concern where child protection authorities had decided that a woman was not allowed to keep her baby following birth."]},{"k":"p","s":["As one participant described:"]},{"k":"p","s":["Certain women – rightfully or wrongfully – are withdrawing from drugs and not approved to have the child. They already know the child is going to be removed from them. […] That will be taken into consideration in terms of using a closeting chain."]},{"k":"h","s":["Ongoing concerns"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is not a new issue. In 2017, the Victorian ombudsman ",["identified","https://assets.ombudsman.vic.gov.au/assets/Reports/Parliamentary-Reports/1-PDF-Report-Files/Implementing-OPCAT-in-Victoria-report-and-inspection-of-Dame-Phyllis-Frost-Centre.pdf"]," the use of shackles during pregnancy and childbirth as a significant concern in Victorian’s maximum security women’s prison."]},{"k":"p","s":["More recently, a ",["review","https://www.health.gov.au/sites/default/files/2024-12/the-national-review-of-first-nations-health-care-in-prisons-2023-24.pdf"]," commissioned by the federal government identified the use of shackles during childbirth as an example of “certain procedures” that “inhibit access, quality or delivery of health care”."]},{"k":"p","s":["While acknowledging this practice “ ",["causes","https://www.instagram.com/reel/De-wCGrhfpw/?utm_source=ig_web_copy_link&mdxt=MzRlODBiNWFlZA%3D%3D&srtk=MzRlODBiNWFlZA%3D%3D"]," harm and distress”, Labor and the Coalition ",["blocked","https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/15/labor-coalition-bill-banning-shackling-incarcerated-women-ntwnfb"]," independent Senator Lidia Thorpe’s federal bill to ban this practice in October, claiming it was a state issue."]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["United Nations","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2026/10/australia-un-experts-concerned-failure-vote-bills-protecting-women-and"]," has criticised the Australian government’s response."]},{"k":"h","s":["What are the laws?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Very little is known about pregnancy or childbirth in Australian prisons, but best estimates suggest that between ",["2%","https://correctiveservices.dcj.nsw.gov.au/about-us/womens-strategy.html"]," and 6% of women will be pregnant during a period of incarceration, with higher estimates among ",["First Nations","https://link.springer.com/article/10.1186/s40352-018-0060-y"]," women."]},{"k":"p","s":["The use of shackles during pregnancy, childbirth and immediately following the birth of a baby is not banned anywhere in Australia. The ",["Guiding Principles for Corrections in Australia","https://files.corrections.vic.gov.au/2025-11/Guiding%20Principles%20for%20Corrections%20in%20Australia%202025.pdf"]," states that “instruments of restraint are not used on prisoners during and immediately following childbirth”. Pregnancy is not explicitly mentioned in that document."]},{"k":"p","s":["Most state and territory correctional policies on the use of shackles are not publicly available. The ones that are ",["available","https://www.corrections.vic.gov.au/commissioners-requirements/section-3/341-living-with-mum-program"]," allow for the use of restraints “with approval from the prison general manager, and in exceptional circumstances only”."]},{"k":"h","s":["A violation of human rights"]},{"k":"p","s":["Shackling women during pregnancy, childbirth or post-birth is a violation of human rights."]},{"k":"p","s":["It contravenes key provisions of the ",["International Covenant on Civil and Political Rights","https://www.ohchr.org/en/instruments-mechanisms/instruments/international-covenant-civil-and-political-rights"],", including the prohibition against torture or cruel, inhuman or degrading treatment or punishment (Article 7) and the presumption that all incarcerated people should be treated with humanity and respect (Article 10)."]},{"k":"p","s":["It also contravenes the UN Rules on the Treatment of Women Prisoners and Non-Custodial Measures for Women Offenders (known as “ ",["the Bangkok Rules","https://www.unodc.org/documents/justice-and-prison-reform/Bangkok_Rules_ENG_22032015.pdf"],"”), which stipulate that instruments of restraint shall not be used during labour, childbirth or immediately after birth."]},{"k":"p","s":["As a signatory to both conventions, Australia has a responsibility to uphold these principles."]},{"k":"p","s":["Shackles during pregnancy, childbirth and post-birth can also pose significant health and ",["medical","https://obgyn.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/1471-0528.17137"]," risks to the mother and her unborn and/or newborn child."]},{"k":"p","s":["This use of restraints is widely opposed by peak medical ",["bodies","https://rcm.org.uk/news/2025/04/rcm-calls-for-urgent-investigation-into-unlawful-restraints-on-pregnant-women-in-prison/"],", including the ",["Congress of Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Nurses and Midwives","https://catsinam.org.au/Common/Uploaded%20files/Smart%20Suite/Smart%20Library/ad73074e-cd42-4022-81bf-0d0cae155393/CATSINaM%20Position%20Statement%20-%20Every%20Woman"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is a visibly degrading practice that causes significant trauma and distress at a time when women are already vulnerable."]},{"k":"p","s":["The impacts on First Nations women, and women from other racialised backgrounds, is likely to be even more ",["severe","https://link.springer.com/article/10.1186/s12939-020-1155-3"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is no evidence, either nationally or internationally, that imprisoned women pose an elevated “flight risk” during or following birth, nor that they pose an unacceptable risk to the safety of others while in hospital. Evidence instead shows it’s time to ban this degrading and unsafe practice."]},{"k":"p","s":["* All names have been changed to protect privacy."]}],"chars":5500},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/angola":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T16:16Z","sha":"2734024dacdf22160f2848402e7888d201a1ad2e79bfed35dd0bdefe20f6019d","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/angola","bytes":59274,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Angola travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-03-14T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-05-28T11:50:56+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel insurance could be invalidated if you travel against advice from the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Areas where FCDO advises against all but essential travel"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Cabinda Province, except Cabinda city"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to Cabinda Province, except to Cabinda city. This is due to separatist groups carrying out targeted attacks on foreigners and the risk of kidnap."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Border areas in Lunda Norte Province"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to within 1km of the border with the Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC) in Lunda Norte province, except for official border crossings and their access roads. This is due to poor conditions, insecurity and banditry."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["why FCDO advises against travel","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/angola/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/angola/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Angola’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Angola set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, check with the Angolan immigration department or contact the ",["Consulate General of Angola in the UK","https://consuladogeralangola-uk.org/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you arrive in Angola and have at least 2 blank pages."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual Citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You do not need a visa to visit Angola for up to 30 days, if visiting for tourism."]},{"k":"p","s":["If travelling for work, study or business, you must ",["get a visa in advance","https://consuladogeralangola-uk.org/vistos/"],". If you do not have a visa, or if you have the wrong visa, you may be stopped from boarding or detained at the airport on arrival. Angola’s deportation process can take a long time."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can be fined 15,000 Angolan kwanzas a day if you overstay your visa. You may not be allowed to leave the country until your fine has been paid. You may also not be allowed to re-enter Angola."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Angolan authorities can fine you for visa offences, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["working, studying or living in Angola without the correct visa"]},{"k":"li","s":["changing employment without notifying the authorities"]},{"k":"li","s":["employing staff with incorrect visas"]},{"k":"li","s":["failing to renew residence cards"]},{"k":"li","s":["changing address without notifying the authorities"]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a risk of yellow fever transmission in Angola. This means you will need a certificate of yellow fever vaccination for some onward travel, including to South Africa."]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about health entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Angola guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/7/angola#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about goods you can take into or out of Angola. You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking money into and out of Angola"]},{"k":"p","s":["Declare cash or travellers cheques if the value is 5,000 US dollars or more (10,000 if you’re a resident). You’ll get a certified declaration to show you brought it in with you."]},{"k":"p","s":["You cannot take out more than 5,000 US dollars (10,000 if you’re a resident) or its equivalent in any foreign currency."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can take out up to 50,000 kwanzas in cash in addition to the foreign currency."]},{"k":"p","s":["Officials at the airport may search you to make sure you’re not leaving the country with more than the allowed amount."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"p","s":["This guide also has safety advice for ",["regions of Angola","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/angola/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Angola"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although there’s no recent history of terrorism in Angola, attacks cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"h","s":["Protests and demonstrations"]},{"k":"p","s":["Public gatherings and demonstrations can occur with little notice and can quickly turn violent. In recent years, there have been protests against the increase in fuel prices and cost of living. In July 2025 there were 3 days of violent riots. Similar protests cannot be ruled out in future."]},{"k":"p","s":["To minimise your personal risk:"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow local media for news of any planned protests"]},{"k":"li","s":["stay away from areas where protests are planned"]},{"k":"li","s":["leave quickly and do not attempt to watch or photograph any demonstration or disturbance"]},{"k":"li","s":["consider making contingency plans"]},{"k":"li","s":["keep a stock of essential supplies"]},{"k":"li","s":["keep your travel documents up-to-date, including appropriate visas"]},{"k":"li","s":["be prepared to move or go into curfew at short notice if told to by the authorities"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["how to prepare for a crisis overseas","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high level of crime in Luanda, some of it violent. Muggers can be armed and some attacks have been fatal. If you are attacked, hand over your money and valuables immediately."]},{"k":"p","s":["Most international companies and organisations operating in Angola have security rules for staff. If your company has rules, read and follow them."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting yourself and your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Criminals target areas popular with foreigners. You should be particularly careful when withdrawing money from banks and ATMs, as you could be followed and robbed."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can reduce your personal risk by:"]},{"k":"li","s":["using pre-arranged cars or hotel cars when withdrawing money"]},{"k":"li","s":["not walking around in Luanda, especially not alone or after dark"]},{"k":"li","s":["not wearing expensive-looking jewellery or watches or using a mobile in public places"]},{"k":"li","s":["not walking between bars and restaurants on the Ilha do Cabo"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoiding crowded places like markets and all large gatherings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Put your valuables and cash in a hotel safe where practical. Keep a ",["certified copy of your passport’s photo page","https://www.gov.uk/certifying-a-document"]," in a separate place."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Vehicle crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Theft from stationary or slow-moving cars is common in downtown Luanda. Keep valuables out of sight and do not use mobiles or laptops while in traffic. When driving, keep doors locked and windows closed. Do not respond if anyone signals you to pull over. Thieves may fake a minor traffic incident to get you out of your car. If they succeed, they may rob you and also steal the car."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sexual assault"]},{"k":"p","s":["Incidents of rape have been reported in popular nightlife areas, as well as in private homes. Never travel alone at night."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["Always carry ID – it is safest to carry a ",["certified copy your passport’s photo page","https://www.gov.uk/certifying-a-document"],". If travelling outside of Luanda and the provincial capitals, take the originals with you, packed as securely as you can. If you do not have any ID, you may get an on-the-spot fine of 15,000 kwanzas."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["Drug taking and smuggling are offences. Punishments can be severe and prison conditions are very poor."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Using cameras and binoculars in secure areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not use cameras, binoculars or GPS equipment near any government buildings. Taking photographs in the streets can draw the attention of the authorities and they may confiscate your camera."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["In January 2019, Angola’s parliament made it illegal to discriminate against people on the basis of sexual orientation. However, public attitudes towards same-sex relationships are less tolerant than in the UK. Showing affection in public may attract negative attention."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Wildlife, animal products and souvenirs"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re caught buying or trafficking goods made of ivory it’s likely you’ll be prosecuted and get a prison sentence or fine."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Angola, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],". Road conditions vary significantly, particularly outside major urban centres, where infrastructure may be poor and emergency response capacity limited. For longer journeys, the use of a roadworthy 4-wheel drive vehicle may be appropriate due to terrain and road conditions. Travellers should use well-maintained vehicles from reputable providers. Outside major urban centres, foreign visitors usually travel in convoys of at least 2 vehicles for safety and in case of breakdowns. Where possible, avoid travelling at night due to poor road conditions, limited street lighting, and reduced access to timely assistance in an emergency."]},{"k":"p","s":["Although you can drive on a UK photocard licence for up to 30 days, it is helpful to get the ",["1949 version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," as well. Make sure you have your driving licence, IDP, and ownership and insurance documents in the car. You will need to show them at the frequent police checkpoints."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road conditions and landmines"]},{"k":"p","s":["Roads outside Luanda and the provincial capitals are often in poor condition. Landmines and unexploded bombs and weapons are still a problem on roads, verges and bridges."]},{"k":"p","s":["During the rainy season from November to April there is an increased chance of mines shifting due to flooding and resurfacing outside known mine fields."]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been incidents where mines have exploded with loss of life in places previously thought to be safe. Even in ‘cleared’ areas, keep to well-established routes and take up-to-date advice from the United Nations or an international non-governmental organisation."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taxis and minibuses"]},{"k":"p","s":["Taxi apps are widely used in Angola. Whilst companies have made efforts to enhance passenger and driver safety these measures can vary. This can result in inconsistent safety and security standards, variable vehicle condition, and limited traceability in the event of an incident. We recommend against using taxi apps where possible. Passengers who choose to do so should always exercise caution and heightened situational awareness. Before entering a vehicle, check the driver’s identity and vehicle details match those provided in the app, share the details with a trusted contact, and avoid sharing rides with unknown individuals. Local minibus and coach transport is considered unsafe and should be avoided."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Air travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["UK Air Safety List (ASL)","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/uk-air-safety-list#angola"]," lists all known airlines in Angola that do not meet international safety standards and are banned from operating commercial air services to and from the UK. Check the UK Air Safety List when considering which airlines to fly with. The list is maintained by the Department for Transport, based on advice from the ",["UK Civil Aviation Authority","https://www.caa.co.uk/Commercial-Industry/Airlines/Licensing/Requirements-and-guidance/Third-Country-Operator-Certificates"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to ",["prepare for and respond to extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Flooding"]},{"k":"p","s":["During the rainy season from November to April, there are storms and heavy downpours. This can cause sudden, serious flooding in and around cities, including Luanda. Flooding can damage roads, buildings and bridges. Stay indoors during storms."]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["This section has safety advice for regions of Angola. It only covers regions where the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) has specific advice."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also read ",["FCDO’s overall travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/angola"]," and ",["safety and security advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/angola/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Cabinda Province, except Cabinda city"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to Cabinda Province, except to Cabinda city."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are regular violent incidents including rape, murder and kidnappings in Cabinda Province. These have involved both foreigners and Angolans."]},{"k":"p","s":["Separatist groups in the northern exclave of Cabinda (a province not joined to the rest of Angola) have been known to carry out attacks involving both foreigners and Angolans. Groups claiming responsibility for these attacks have said they’ll continue attacks against foreigners."]},{"k":"h","s":["Border areas in Lunda Norte Province"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to within 1km of the border with the Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC) in Lunda Norte province, except for official border crossings and their access roads."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO also advises against all travel to the provinces of Kasaï and Kasaï Central, across the border in the ",["Central Democratic Republic of Congo","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/democratic-republic-of-the-congo"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["The rest of Lunda Norte and Lunda Sul"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against travelling to Lunda Norte and Lunda Sol unless absolutely necessary. Get security advice and travel with the support of a security company or sponsoring organisation."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Angolan authorities are sensitive to the presence of foreigners in diamond-producing areas, which includes Lunda Norte and Lunda Sul. They may impose restrictions on your movement in these provinces. If you do not comply, they may arrest you and detain you."]},{"k":"p","s":["The diamond mines increase the threat of crime and banditry on roads leading to and from these areas. Bandits may carry out armed hold-ups."]},{"k":"h","s":["Areas outside Luanda and the provincial capitals"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you travel outside Luanda and the provincial capitals, go with people or organisations that know the area, as conditions can be difficult. There is widespread poverty, limited infrastructure, and social exclusion and disease. There are mines and unexploded weapons in many parts of the country."]},{"k":"p","s":["Transport and accommodation are extremely limited outside Luanda. Officials are likely to ask for your passport and visa or entry stamp, so take the originals with you."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 112 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Angola","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/7/angola#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Angola","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/7/angola"]," including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Yellow fever"]},{"k":"li","s":["Malaria and dengue"]},{"k":"li","s":["Zika virus"]},{"k":"li","s":["Cholera"]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a risk in parts of Angola. Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Ebola"]},{"k":"p","s":["On 15 May the Democratic Republic of Congo Ministry of Health announced an outbreak of Ebola Bundibugyo in the North-Eastern Ituri Province. Read more about the ",["Ebola outbreak on TravelHealth Pro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/63/democratic-republic-of-the-congo#Outbreaks"]," and see ",["information on Ebola and similar diseases.","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/68/viral-haemorrhagic-fever"]," World Health Organisation (WHO) have ",["declared this a Public Health Emergency of International Concern","https://www.who.int/news/item/17-05-2026-epidemic-of-ebola-disease-in-the-democratic-republic-of-the-congo-and-uganda-determined-a-public-health-emergency-of-international-concern"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Due to the outbreak, you may experience heightened health screening at international borders in the region. ",["Check entry requirements","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice"]," for the country you’re travelling to or transiting."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Angola"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are several competent private clinics in Luanda. They charge high fees in advance. Outside Luanda healthcare is very limited. Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment abroad and repatriation."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in Angola","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/list-of-medical-facilities-and-funeral-directors-in-angola/angola-list-of-medical-facilities"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Angola"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: 112"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 118"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 110"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Angola"]," and ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Angola"]," in Angola"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Angola","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/bereavement-information-for-angola/angola-bereavement-information--2"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Angola","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/angola-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/angola/british-embassy-luanda"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/angola/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Angola","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-angola"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":18115,"change":"Addition of information about a declaration of an Ebola outbreak in DRC on 15 May and updated information about road travel ('Safety and security' and 'Health' pages)."},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/hong-kong":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T16:30Z","sha":"4efde29d74531e084cf7dee061314f49f576084a0dd2ac5b8dc245bf6dfde8c9","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/hong-kong","bytes":81525,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Hong Kong (SAR of China) travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-03-01T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-04-01T16:59:28+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["This travel advice covers the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region (SAR). For mainland China, see ",["travel advice for China","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/china"]," and for Macao SAR, see ",["Macao travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/macao"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual Chinese-British nationality"]},{"k":"p","s":["Hong Kong does not recognise dual nationality, and does not recognise the BN(O) passport as a valid travel document or proof of identity. If you hold both British and Chinese nationality, local authorities may treat you solely as a Chinese citizen, even if you enter Hong Kong on a full “British citizen” passport or hold a British National (Overseas) passport. In such circumstances, the British Consulate-General may not be able to offer you consular assistance."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you have formally renounced Chinese citizenship, carry evidence that you have done so."]},{"k":"p","s":["See guidance on ",["nationality in China","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/nationality-in-china"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/hong-kong/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Hong Kong’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Hong Kong set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact ",["Hong Kong’s Economic and Trade Office in the UK","https://www.hketolondon.gov.hk/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Hong Kong no longer accept BN(O) passports for immigration clearance and do not recognise them as valid proof of identity."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your passport must be valid for at least one month after the date you plan to leave Hong Kong."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Other types of ",["British nationals who are exempt from ETA","https://www.gov.uk/eta/when-not-need-eta"]," must also carry a valid British passport when entering the UK."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["Hong Kong is part of the People’s Republic of China, but it is a Special Administrative Region (SAR) with its own immigration controls."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can visit Hong Kong for up to 6 months without a visa. For information on entry requirements see the ",["Hong Kong SAR government website","https://www.gov.hk/en/nonresidents/visarequire/general/index.htm"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["To stay longer, to work or study, for business travel or for other reasons, you must get a visa. For further information contact the nearest ",["Chinese mission with visa issuing facilities","https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/mfa_eng/wjb_663304/zwjg_665342/"]," or the ",["Hong Kong Immigration Department","https://www.immd.gov.hk/eng/contactus/index.html"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Hong Kong, you must have a certificate to prove you’ve had a yellow fever vaccination if you’re coming from a ",["country listed as a transmission risk","https://nathnacyfzone.org.uk/factsheet/65/countries-with-risk-of-yellow-fever-transmission"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Hong Kong guide","https://www.travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/102/hong-kong-china#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into or out of Hong Kong","https://www.customs.gov.hk/en/service-enforcement-information/passenger-clearance/prohibited-controlled-items/index.html"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty. Children aged 3 and over must follow the same rules as adult travellers unless otherwise stated."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Bringing restricted items into Hong Kong"]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s illegal for visitors arriving in Hong Kong International Airport to carry items including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["stun guns"]},{"k":"li","s":["objects with sharp points or edges (for example, samurai swords)"]},{"k":"li","s":["martial arts equipment (for example, knuckledusters)"]},{"k":"p","s":["You could be fined or given a prison sentence. See further information from the ",["Hong Kong Police Force","https://www.police.gov.hk/ppp_en/04_crime_matters/cpa/cpa_at_01.html"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["E-cigarettes"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is prohibited to bring e-cigarettes, heated tobacco products, herbal cigarettes, or related devices into Hong Kong, including in personal luggage. From 30 April 2026, possessing any e-cigarette or “Alternative Smoking Product” (ASP) in a public place will be illegal, regardless of whether it is in use. Offences also include selling, manufacturing, promoting, advertising, or possessing e-cigarettes for commercial purposes. Possession of these items or their components can result in imprisonment and substantial fines. Travellers transiting through Hong Kong without passing immigration control are exempt from these restrictions."]},{"k":"hs","s":["CBD (cannabidiol)"]},{"k":"p","s":["Hong Kong classifies CBD as a dangerous drug. All cannabis products are illegal in Hong Kong, including CBD (cannabidiol) items such as oils, creams, capsules, and food products."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Powdered baby formula"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are restrictions on the amount of powdered baby formula you can take out of Hong Kong. If you do not follow the rules, you could face a fine or imprisonment for up to 2 years."]},{"k":"p","s":["See more information, including exemptions, from the ",["Hong Kong Customs and Excise Department","https://www.customs.gov.hk/en/service-enforcement-information/trade-facilitation/prohibited-articles/controlled-exports/index.html"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Hong Kong"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorist attacks in Hong Kong cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protests and civil unrest"]},{"k":"p","s":["Between 2019 and 2020, large-scale political demonstrations took place in Hong Kong, including popular tourist areas. There were some violent clashes between police and protesters."]},{"k":"p","s":["Protests are rare but could take place at any time. If you are near a demonstration, follow the advice of local authorities and move away to a safe place."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting yourself and your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Violent crime is low but pickpocketing and other street crime can happen. Take extra care of passports, credit cards and money in crowded areas and when checking in and out of hotels."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you plan to hike in Hong Kong’s country parks, stay on the marked trails and do not carry valuables."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Drink spiking and sexual assault"]},{"k":"p","s":["Personal attacks, including sexual assaults, are rare but do happen, including by drink spiking. Do not leave drinks unattended and do not accept drinks from strangers. Women travelling alone, or with other females, could be at greater risk. See ",["advice for women travelling abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["National security laws"]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["2020 National Security Law (NSL)","https://www.gld.gov.hk/egazette/english/gazette/volume.php?year=2020&vol=24&no=48&extra=1&type=0"]," includes offences such as:"]},{"k":"li","s":["secession"]},{"k":"li","s":["subversion"]},{"k":"li","s":["organisation and perpetration of terrorist activities"]},{"k":"li","s":["collusion with a foreign country"]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["2024 Safeguarding National Security Ordinance","https://www.sb.gov.hk/eng/bl23/consultation.html"]," includes offences such as:"]},{"k":"li","s":["treason"]},{"k":"li","s":["sedition"]},{"k":"li","s":["unlawful disclosure of state secrets"]},{"k":"li","s":["external interference endangering national security"]},{"k":"p","s":["National security laws can be interpreted broadly and some offences can lead to a maximum penalty of life imprisonment. Individuals and organisations can be prosecuted and are required to comply with national security investigations, including sharing full access to electronic devices."]},{"k":"p","s":["The national security laws apply to activities taking place inside and outside Hong Kong, including in the UK. The national security laws apply to all individuals regardless of nationality or residency."]},{"k":"p","s":["Hong Kong’s National Security Police have issued arrest warrants and financial rewards against individuals living outside Hong Kong, including in the UK under the 2020 National Security Law."]},{"k":"p","s":["You could be detained or removed to mainland China for some offences under the 2020 National Security Law."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Criticising the government"]},{"k":"p","s":["Some people have been prosecuted for publishing or supporting statements that are critical of the Hong Kong or Chinese authorities, including online. You could also be prosecuted for supporting individuals who are considered to be breaking national security laws."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Immigration Ordinance"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Immigration (Amendment) Ordinance came into force in 2021. Under this law, people could be stopped from leaving the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region (SAR). However, the Hong Kong SAR government has said these powers will only be used to stop certain asylum seekers from entering Hong Kong."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Public offences"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can get on-the-spot fines for littering, jay walking or spitting."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Wildlife, animal products and souvenirs"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to import and re-export elephant ivory and its products, including tourist souvenirs. You could get a fine or prison sentence."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs"]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid any involvement with illegal drugs, including cannabis. All cannabis products are illegal in Hong Kong, including CBD (cannabidiol) items such as oils, creams, capsules, and food products."]},{"k":"p","s":["Criminal gangs and individuals in the UK and overseas have been known to coerce people into carrying drugs. Do not allow yourself to be persuaded."]},{"k":"p","s":["Hong Kong enforces a zero‑tolerance policy toward dangerous drugs and will not tolerate drug‑related activities. If you are found guilty of smuggling, trafficking, possessing, or using illegal narcotics, including while transiting through the airport, you should expect a severe prison sentence."]},{"k":"p","s":["Airports in Hong Kong have excellent technology and security for detecting illegal items. This is also used to scan the baggage of transiting passengers."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking photographs in secure areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not take photographs of military installations."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are visiting, you can drive in Hong Kong with a valid UK driving licence for up to 12 months."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are living in Hong Kong, see the ",["Hong Kong SAR Transport Department","https://www.td.gov.hk/en/public_services/licences_and_permits/driving_licences/how_to_apply_for_a_driving_licence/driving_in_hong_kong_for_overseas_driving_licence_/index.html"]," for information on applying for a full or temporary driving licence."]},{"k":"p","s":["Hire car companies often have stricter requirements for their customers, such as a year of driving experience, a higher minimum age and holding an international driving permit. Check requirements with the car hire company before you travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to ",["prepare for and respond to extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Typhoons"]},{"k":"p","s":["Typhoon season runs from May to November in Hong Kong and may cause flooding and landslides. Follow any local warnings issued in advance. Public offices and public transport will shut down when there is a ‘Typhoon 8’ storm signal."]},{"k":"p","s":["Monitor local news and check the ",["World Meteorological Organization","https://severeweather.wmo.int/tc/wnp/index.html"]," and ",["Hong Kong Observatory","https://www.hko.gov.hk/en/index.html"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 999 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Hong Kong","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/102/hong-kong-china#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Hong Kong","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/102/hong-kong-china"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Hong Kong"]},{"k":"p","s":["Medical treatment for uninsured foreign visitors to Hong Kong is expensive. You can only get prescribed medication through a doctor unless your UK prescription specifically says the medication will be required in Hong Kong."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a list of ",["medical providers in Hong Kong","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/hong-kong-list-of-medical-facilities"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is also ",["guidance on healthcare if you’re living in Hong Kong","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/living-in-hong-kong#health"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Hong Kong"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 999 (ambulance, fire, police)"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Hong%20Kong"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Hong%20Kong"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Hong%20Kong"]," in Hong Kong"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Hong Kong","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/bereavement-information-for-hong-kong/hong-kong-bereavement-information"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Hong Kong","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/hong-kong-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/hong-kong/british-consulate-general-hong-kong"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/hong-kong/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk guidance offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Hong Kong","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-hong-kong"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":14300,"change":"Updated information on dual Chinese-British nationality, E-cigarettes and illegal drugs including CBD (cannabidiol) (‘Warnings and insurance’, ‘Entry requirements’ and ‘Safety and security’ pages)."},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kazakhstan":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T17:03Z","sha":"d95fd769e61f222dbc15bbf2aad8a0227528e0d827e242197a64c46983ea65b1","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/kazakhstan","bytes":63720,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Kazakhstan travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-02-18T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-10-30T14:52:10+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kazakhstan/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Kazakhstan’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Kazakhstan set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Kazakh Embassy in the UK","https://www.gov.kz/memleket/entities/mfa-london?lang=en"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Kazakhstan, your passport must be valid for at least 30 days from the date you arrive and have at least one blank page."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you have a visa for Kazakhstan, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 3 months after your visa’s expiry date."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Kazakh-British dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["Kazakhstan does not recognise dual nationality. If you are found to have a Kazakh passport and another passport, you will be fined and your Kazakh citizenship may be withdrawn."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can visit Kazakhstan without a visa for up to 30 days for business or tourism. You can make as many visa-free visits as you like, but you must not stay more than 90 days without a visa in any 180-day period."]},{"k":"p","s":["To stay longer, to work or study or for other reasons, you must meet the Kazakh government’s entry requirements. Check which type of visa or work permit you need with the ",["Kazakh Embassy in the UK","https://www.gov.kz/memleket/entities/mfa-london?lang=en"],". Also see ",["visa information from Kazakhstan’s Ministry of Foreign Affairs","https://www.gov.kz/memleket/entities/mfa/activities/3053?lang=en&parentId=3051"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Applying for a visa"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can apply for a visa from the ",["Kazakhstan government’s visa website","https://vmp.gov.kz/en/"],". Check the validity dates of your visa and any restrictions before you travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["British nationals aged 17 or over who apply for a visa or residency must submit biometrics (fingerprints) as part of the application process."]},{"k":"h","s":["Electronic Travel Authorisation (ETA)"]},{"k":"p","s":["From 1 November, if you travel to Kazakhstan without a visa, you should apply for an Electronic Travel Authorisation (ETA) through the ",["QazETA portal","https://qazeta.kz/en"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["During the transition period between 1 November and 30 June, if you do not have an ETA, you will not be refused entry but will be informed of this requirement when entering Kazakhstan."]},{"k":"p","s":["From 1 July 2027, the ETA will become mandatory for all visa-free nationals and you will be refused entry if you do not have one."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should apply at least 72 hours before travel. The ETA is free of charge and is valid for 180 days from the date of issue."]},{"k":"p","s":["An ETA does not extend the length of your permitted visa-free stay and does not replace any existing visa requirements."]},{"k":"p","s":["You do not need an ETA if you are:"]},{"k":"li","s":["under 16 years old or over 65 years old"]},{"k":"li","s":["transiting through Kazakhstan and remaining in the transit area of an international airport without crossing the border"]},{"k":"li","s":["travelling on a diplomatic or service passport"]},{"k":"li","s":["a holder of a valid Kazakh visa or residence permit"]},{"k":"p","s":["A full list of exemptions can be found in the FAQs section of the ",["QazETA portal","https://qazeta.kz/en/faq"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Registering with the authorities"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your hotel or the person hosting you must ",["register your arrival with the Kazakh authorities","https://vmp.gov.kz/en/services/notice-service"],". They must do this within 3 working days of your arrival in Kazakhstan."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travelling overland between Kazakhstan, Kyrgyzstan, Russia and Belarus"]},{"k":"p","s":["Kazakhstan, Kyrgyzstan, Russia and Belarus are in a single customs union. If you want to travel overland in your own vehicle between these countries, make sure your customs declaration and temporary import licence are valid for your whole stay in all 4 countries. You can extend the import licence for up to one year by contacting the customs authorities in any of the countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["Kyrgyzstan travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kyrgyzstan"],", ",["Russia travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/russia"]," and ",["Belarus travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/belarus"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Kazakhstan, you must have a certificate to prove you’ve had a yellow fever vaccination if you’re coming from a ",["country listed as a transmission risk","https://nathnacyfzone.org.uk/factsheet/65/countries-with-risk-of-yellow-fever-transmission"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Kazakhstan guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/116/kazakhstan#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into or out of Kazakhstan","https://egov.kz/cms/en/articles/customs/rules-for-importing-goods"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking money into Kazakhstan"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are limits on ",["how much foreign currency you can bring","https://egov.kz/cms/en/articles/customs/rules-for-importing-goods"]," to Kazakhstan or take with you when you leave."]},{"k":"p","s":["You must declare to customs authorities if you arrive in Kazakhstan with cash of a value greater than 10,000 US dollars. If you do not declare it the funds may be confiscated, and you may receive a fine."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is not permitted to export any foreign currency in cash of a value greater than 10,000 US dollars. If such a value is declared it may only be exported in Kazakh tenge."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact the ",["State Revenue Department","https://kgd.gov.kz/en/node/66966"]," if you have specific questions."]},{"k":"hs","s":["IMEI registration"]},{"k":"p","s":["To use a local SIM card, you must verify your device’s IMEI at ",["imei.kz portal","https://kz-imei.kz/landing-page"],". This requires a border‑crossing certificate obtained from the ",["QazETA mobile app","https://www.vmp.gov.kz/en/"]," and a Kazakh Individual Identification Number (IIN). If you do not verify, your local SIM card will be blocked after 30 days, and you will not be able to activate another one."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you cannot verify your device’s IMEI and your stay exceeds 30 days, consider using a global eSIM instead."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Kazakhstan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorist attacks in Kazakhstan cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"p","s":["Attacks could be indiscriminate, including in places visited by foreign nationals. Be alert for any security related announcements by the Kazakh authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["Public demonstrations are only permitted when authorised by the Kazakh authorities in advance. Occasional unauthorised small-scale public protests take place. Attending unauthorised demonstrations or political gatherings may put participants at risk of arrest."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Robbery and violent crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been violent thefts in expatriate communities in Atyrau and Aktau in western Kazakhstan and in Astana and Almaty. They happen mainly at night in and around local nightclubs and bars or when arriving home late at night. Robberies are uncommon in cities and rural areas but do happen. Take the same precautions you would in the UK to protect your belongings."]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid walking alone at night and pre-arrange your transport. Do not use unofficial taxis or a taxi already occupied by a passenger."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Pickpocketing is very common in crowded places such as markets and on public transport. Criminals may target foreigners as they are assumed to be carrying valuable items. Keep valuables in a safe place and out of public view."]},{"k":"p","s":["Thieves may target luggage on trains. Always lock your railway compartment on an overnight train."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Bank card fraud"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fraudsters can steal your card details without you noticing. Use ATMs inside banks if possible, and check ATMs on the street for signs of tampering. Keep cards in sight when paying in shops and restaurants. Read ",["more about how to avoid bank card fraud","https://www.actionfraud.police.uk/a-z-of-fraud/bank-card-and-cheque-fraud"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Drink spiking and sexual assault"]},{"k":"p","s":["Drink spiking is a risk in nightclubs and bars and can lead to sexual assault. Alcohol and drugs can reduce your vigilance, making you less in control."]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid splitting up from your friends, do not leave drinks unattended and do not go off with people you do not know. Save the location of your accommodation on your maps app, so it’s easy to find. See ",["TravelAware ‘Stick with your mates’","https://travelaware.campaign.gov.uk/#stick_with_your_mates"]," for tips and advice."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"p","s":["Individuals found guilty of inciting social, national, racial or religious discord may face a lengthy sentence. Insulting another person using abusive language may also result in a court ordered fine or community service. Respect local traditions, customs, laws and religions."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["Carry original ID such as your driving licence or passport at all times. Police patrolling the streets may ask for your ID, and copies are not acceptable. You need to show your original ID to enter state buildings."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Ramadan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ramadan is a holy month for Muslims. The dates vary by year and country. Cafés and restaurants may amend their menus and be busy around fast-breaking (‘Iftar’). Areas around mosques are also likely to be busy around prayer times. Take particular care not to offend religious sensitivities at this time."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Alcohol laws and bans"]},{"k":"p","s":["The drinking age in Kazakhstan is 18. However, it is illegal to sell alcohol to someone aged 20 or under. You may be refused the sale of alcohol if you are unable to present a valid proof of age ID on request."]},{"k":"p","s":["Shops are not allowed to sell alcohol between 11pm and 8am. Alcoholic drinks which have an alcohol content level of more than 30% cannot be sold in shops between 9pm and 12 noon. Bars, restaurants and cafés are not covered by this rule."]},{"k":"p","s":["If police find you drinking alcohol in the street, or if you appear to be drunk, they can take you to a police station and issue you with a fine or detain you in a police cell overnight."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Smoking and e-cigarette bans"]},{"k":"p","s":["Smoking and vaping are illegal in and near to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["schools and playgrounds"]},{"k":"li","s":["healthcare facilities"]},{"k":"li","s":["public places – museums, libraries, cinemas, sport centres, public transport, nightclubs, airports, rail stations and underpasses"]},{"k":"li","s":["cars with children travelling"]},{"k":"p","s":["The fine for smoking in an unauthorised place is around £90, and more if it’s a repeat offence."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to sell, distribute, import or produce smokeless cigarettes, e-cigarettes (vapes), or e-liquid for e-cigarettes. You could get a fine or a prison sentence of up to 2 years."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs"]},{"k":"p","s":["Illegal drugs, including cannabis, carry severe penalties. You should expect a long jail sentence and heavy fines for possessing, using or smuggling illegal drugs, including when transiting through the airport."]},{"k":"p","s":["You could face a lengthy prison sentence:"]},{"k":"li","s":["for possession, storing and transportation of drugs with distribution purposes – 5 to 8 years"]},{"k":"li","s":["for possession, storing and transportation of drugs with distribution purposes in large amounts – 6 to 10 years"]},{"k":"li","s":["for advertising drugs – up to 3 years in prison, and 3 to 6 years if using social media"]},{"k":"p","s":["Prison conditions are basic."]},{"k":"p","s":["Airports in Kazakhstan have excellent technology and security for detecting illegal items. This is also used to scan the baggage of transiting passengers."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Posting on social media"]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s illegal to post images or comments on social media that show disrespect towards religion, culture or national symbols. Take particular care with images that show the Kazakh flag. Sharing or publishing images that the authorities consider to be insulting risks a fine or a prison sentence."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking photos in secure areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are restrictions on where you can take photos or videos, especially near military sites, border areas, airports and some official buildings. Restrictions may be in force despite a lack of warning signs. Taking photographs of sensitive sites risks confiscation of your equipment."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some large shops and supermarkets do not allow photography."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Using drones in Kazakhstan"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can bring a drone to Kazakhstan without a licence. However, you risk a fine, detention and the confiscation of your drone if you operate a drone without a licence."]},{"k":"p","s":["Apply for a drone licence from the Civil Aviation Committee. You should include technical characteristics of the drone and details of planned use (when, where and how long). See local regulations on ",["drone licensing requirements","https://adilet.zan.kz/rus/docs/V2000022031"]," (in Russian)."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Money"]},{"k":"p","s":["Only change money at banks or officially authorised currency exchanges. You will be required to present your passport for identification."]},{"k":"p","s":["Official exchange booths may not accept damaged or marked bank notes, or US dollars issued before 2013."]},{"k":"p","s":["Depending on your bank, you may be able to withdraw cash in Kazakhstani tenge (KZT) from ATMs using an international debit or credit card. Availability and fees may vary, so it is advisable to check with your bank before travelling."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex sexual activity is not illegal in Kazakhstan. However, on 30 December 2025, legislation was introduced prohibiting the ‘promotion’ or dissemination of information about non-traditional sexual orientation. Perceived breaches of this law may result in administrative penalties, including fines, detention, and deportation."]},{"k":"p","s":["Public acceptance of LGBT+ people and identities in Kazakhstan is limited, especially outside major cities. There is an increased risk of discrimination or harassment against individuals thought to be part of the LGBT+ community, or perceived to be supporting their rights."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Wildlife, animal products and souvenirs"]},{"k":"p","s":["You are not allowed to export:"]},{"k":"li","s":["art or antiques that have historical, cultural or scientific value"]},{"k":"li","s":["gold, precious stones or rare minerals"]},{"k":"li","s":["rare specimens of flora or animals"]},{"k":"p","s":["Take local expert advice before making any such purchase."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Trekking and mountaineering"]},{"k":"p","s":["Trekking in Kazakhstan often involves travelling to very remote areas. There is a high risk of avalanches, landslides and rockfalls. Weather can change very quickly, and heavy snowfall can block roads and trekking routes, particularly in the autumn and winter."]},{"k":"p","s":["At higher altitudes there is a possibility of snow even in the summer months, and a risk of sunstroke, serious sunburn and altitude sickness."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["get adequate insurance, including for any activity at high altitude"]},{"k":"li","s":["use a reputable trekking agency"]},{"k":"li","s":["let someone know when you plan to return"]},{"k":"li","s":["not trek alone"]},{"k":"li","s":["adapt your plans to reflect local conditions and advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["In remote areas, mobile phone or satellite phone coverage can be extremely limited. Medical facilities are basic, and difficult terrain can in some circumstances make it impossible for emergency services to reach you."]},{"k":"p","s":["The 24-hour rescue services in Almaty are based in Shymbulak gorge and by the Big Almaty lake. A rescue team patrols mountain routes, searches for missing persons and provides first aid. The Almaty emergency numbers are 109 or 112."]},{"k":"p","s":["Almaty city authorities have installed 18 refuges in remote mountain areas where tourists can find shelter, access first aid kits and SOS buttons to contact the emergency services."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Kazakhstan, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"]," and ",["Kazakhstan’s rules of the road","https://adilet.zan.kz/rus/docs/Z1400000194"]," (in Russian)."]},{"k":"p","s":["You need a ",["1968 international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," as well as your UK licence to drive in Kazakhstan. You cannot buy an IDP outside the UK, so get one before you travel. Check if you need a ",["UK sticker to drive your car outside the UK","https://www.gov.uk/displaying-number-plates/flags-identifiers-and-stickers"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The minimum legal age for driving is 16 for motorbikes and 18 for cars."]},{"k":"p","s":["Hire car companies often have stricter requirements for their customers, such as a year of driving experience, a higher minimum age and holding an IDP."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taxis"]},{"k":"p","s":["To avoid accidentally using an unlicenced taxi or being overcharged, avoid flagging down taxis and use licensed pre-ordered taxi services whenever possible."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road conditions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Driving standards can be erratic. Many cars are not safely maintained and do not have rear seatbelts."]},{"k":"p","s":["When driving in Kazakhstan do not take risks and avoid driving in bad weather. Many roads are poorly maintained. Roadworks and damaged roads are often not signposted. In remote rural areas, there are often stray animals on the roads. In winter, roads can be hazardous due to snow or ice, and low visibility can lead to accidents involving multiple cars."]},{"k":"p","s":["Service stations are limited outside the main cities. Take all that you need for your journey, including fuel and water. Make sure your vehicle is properly maintained and in a good condition for long journeys."]},{"k":"p","s":["If traffic police stop you for a traffic offence, they should give you an official paper."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow local advice on road closures. Local sim cards will receive updates in Kazakh and Russian from 112, and alerts are provided in English on the ",["QazAvtoJol","https://en.qaj.kz/"]," website."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Closed areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["The following areas are closed to visitors unless you have received prior permission from the Foreign Ministry, the Interior Ministry and the Kazakh National Security Committee:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Gvardeyskiy village in the Almaty region of south-eastern Kazakhstan"]},{"k":"li","s":["the town of Baikonur"]},{"k":"li","s":["the districts of Karmakchi and Kazalinsk in the southern Kyzylorda region"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Border crossings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Officials in Kazakhstan or neighbouring countries may close border crossing points at short notice. If you are travelling overland be alert for any announcements by the Kazakh authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to ",["prepare for and respond to extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Wildfires"]},{"k":"p","s":["Wildfires affected forests in east Kazakhstan in 2023. Regions in the Kazakh steppe can also be affected by grass fires. Take local advice."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Flooding and mudslides"]},{"k":"p","s":["Widespread flooding affected much of northern and western Kazakhstan in April 2024. Take local advice about road closures and transport disruption caused by flooding."]},{"k":"p","s":["Mudslides and landslides can occur in the mountain areas of south-east Kazakhstan."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Kazakhstan has several areas which are at high risk of earthquakes. Almaty is in an active seismic zone."]},{"k":"p","s":["The US Federal Emergency Management Agency has advice about ",["what to do before, during and after an earthquake","https://www.ready.gov/earthquakes"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dial 103 and ask for an ambulance. The operator answering may not speak English."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Kazakhstan","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/116/kazakhstan#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See what ",["health risks you’ll face in Kazakhstan","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/116/kazakhstan"]," including biting insects and ticks."]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a risk in parts of Kazakhstan. Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Basic medications such as aspirin are available without a prescription. It’s best to bring enough medication with you."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you need prescription medication while in Kazakhstan, you will need a valid prescription either from a local doctor or your UK prescription translated into Kazakh or Russian. Medications often come under different brand names, so ask for the drug’s generic name. If they are not available locally, it may be possible to get drugs to be couriered through a private clinic, for example, International SOS clinic."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Kazakhstan"]},{"k":"p","s":["The medical facilities in Kazakhstan are not as advanced as in the UK. Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of medical treatment or evacuation by air ambulance and repatriation. Medical staff do not typically speak English."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a list of ",["medical facilities in Kazakhstan","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/kazakhstan-list-of-medical-facilities"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Kazakhstan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: 103"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 101"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police:102"]},{"k":"p","s":["Emergency and rescue service: 112"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Kazakhstan"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Kazakhstan"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Kazakhstan"]," in Kazakhstan"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Kazakhstan","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/kazakhstan-bereavement-death-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Kazakhstan","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/kazakhstan-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/kazakhstan/british-embassy-tokyo"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kazakhstan/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Kazakhstan","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-kazakhstan"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":22638,"change":"Updated information about Electronic Travel Authorisation (ETA) ('Entry requirements' page)."},"https://theconversation.com/disproportional-representation-what-national-wins-and-loses-from-the-overhang-296137":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T17:03Z","sha":"e5774f3137f8723961f9eaf70060eada3a48e7dfd026d1a953a6d69bdabf1460","read":"https://theconversation.com/disproportional-representation-what-national-wins-and-loses-from-the-overhang-296137","bytes":181639,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Disproportional representation: what National wins and loses from the overhang","by":[{"n":"Richard Shaw","r":"Professor of Politics, Te Kunenga ki Pūrehuroa – Massey University"}],"pub":"2026-11-10T01:30:26Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Did New Zealand just witness a first-past-the-post election under MMP?"]},{"k":"p","s":["There was a time when elections were determined by results in a handful of marginal electorates. Since the ",["introduction of MMP","https://elections.nz/democracy-in-nz/what-is-new-zealands-system-of-government/what-is-mmp/the-history-of-mmp"]," in 1996, however, overall voter support for individual parties has been the deciding factor."]},{"k":"p","s":["This year, the old days seem to have returned. The outcome could well ",["hinge on a small number of close-run seats","https://www.rnz.co.nz/news/politics_election-2026/2448587/how-399-000-votes-could-cost-christopher-luxon-his-majority"]," – just like ",["pre-proportional elections","https://elections.nz/democracy-in-nz/what-is-new-zealands-system-of-government/what-is-mmp/the-history-of-mmp"]," used to."]},{"k":"p","s":["Put aside questions about who will hold the balance of power when final results are announced on November 27, or whether Christopher Luxon will go back on his word and ",["negotiate with the Opportunity Party","https://www.rnz.co.nz/news/election-2026-results/updates"]," if he has to."]},{"k":"p","s":["Deeper down, the tectonic plates of New Zealand politics are drifting."]},{"k":"h","s":["Rumblings in the electoral system"]},{"k":"p","s":["The next parliament is going to be the largest in history. While it generally numbers between 120 and 123 MPs, the ",["overhangs created on the left and right","https://theconversation.com/nzs-next-government-hangs-in-the-balance-2026-election-results-at-a-glance-295556"]," are so large it could have as many as 131."]},{"k":"p","s":["This will be the sixth overhang since MMP was adopted, but two things set this one apart: its size and its impact."]},{"k":"p","s":["The discrepancy between the parties’ share of the vote and their share of all parliamentary seats will be distorted. That means it will affect the formation of the next government."]},{"k":"p","s":["Without the overhang, provisional results would have given both National and Labour roughly 36 seats. But because National’s performance in the electorates exceeded its showing on the party vote, it currently has 42 seats."]},{"k":"p","s":["This means National holds 32% of seats in a 131-member parliament to Labour’s 27.5% – even though the parties are neck-and-neck on the party vote."]},{"k":"p","s":["This disconnect between vote share and seat share is the sort of thing that fuelled New Zealanders’ ",["rejection of the old first-past-the-post system","https://nzhistory.govt.nz/page/road-mmp"],". In 1978 and 1981, for instance, Labour secured more votes than National overall but lost the election because it won fewer seats."]},{"k":"p","s":["The similarities with the 2026 election are uncanny: on provisional results Labour’s lead over National on the party vote is 3,650 votes; in 1981, Labour’s lead was 4,122."]},{"k":"h","s":["Negatives for National"]},{"k":"p","s":["We’ve seen this coming. Both the ",["2012 MMP Review","https://elections.nz/democracy-in-nz/what-is-new-zealands-system-of-government/what-is-mmp/2012-mmp-review"]," and the ",["2023 Independent Electoral Review","https://www.justice.govt.nz/justice-sector-policy/constitutional-issues-and-human-rights/independent-electoral-review/"]," addressed the overhang issue. Each recommended abolishing the provision for overhang seats – and on both occasions National (or National-led) governments chose not to act on those recommendations."]},{"k":"p","s":["While National would rather return to office than to opposition, the election result presents the party with significant challenges."]},{"k":"p","s":["For one thing, it is now an electorate-only party: voters like the party’s individual MPs ",["more than they like the party itself","https://www.rnz.co.nz/news/politics_election-2026/2486951/they-hate-us-outgoing-national-mp-says-party-has-gone-too-far-to-the-right"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["That has never happened to a major party before in the MMP era, and poses a strategic conundrum for National: does it swing further right to retake the votes it has shed to ACT and New Zealand First, or return to the ground it held when it was a broad-based party of the centre-right?"]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s not clear what influence the ",["vote-splitting campaign","https://splityourvote.co.nz/"]," to deliberately engineer an overhang had on the results. But there was a reason Luxon called strategic voting “ ",["the opposite of clever","https://www.rnz.co.nz/news/politics_election-2026/1631392/act-nz-first-hit-back-at-national-s-warning-against-strategic-voting"],"”: it reduces the party’s influence in coalition negotiations and slashes its presence in the next cabinet."]},{"k":"p","s":["National supporters have also effectively ",["deprived their own party","https://www.rnz.co.nz/news/politics_election-2026/2440697/luxon-defends-his-leadership-after-huge-loss-of-senior-mps"]," of three of its most senior and hard-working ministers. Nicola Willis, Paul Goldsmith and Chris Bishop carry 18 ministerial portfolios between them (some of which will go to ACT or New Zealand First ministers if the same coalition government is eventually returned)."]},{"k":"p","s":["And should National voters develop a taste for strategic voting, the party won’t be able to rely on its list to balance the slate of candidates selected by the party’s electorate committees."]},{"k":"p","s":["Local concerns and national priorities don’t always align. Political parties use their lists to create the desired mix of candidates on the basis of competence, experience, gender, ethnicity and so on."]},{"k":"p","s":["National’s capacity to do this has now been hamstrung. Spare a thought for its campaign manager at the next general election."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["What really drove NZ’s election overhang and what can be done about it","https://theconversation.com/what-really-drove-nzs-election-overhang-and-what-can-be-done-about-it-296144"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Positives for National"]},{"k":"p","s":["On the other hand, National’s performance in the electorates could be a potential long-term advantage."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a strategic case to be made for focusing on electorate contests ( ",["as Te Pāti Māori has done","https://www.nzherald.co.nz/nz/politics/te-pati-maori-told-supporters-to-party-vote-labour-or-green-what-did-they-do/2VQEPJYKDBBGJNOMMSFFQROHVE/"]," in the Māori electorates, and ",["as some German parties do","https://www.firstpost.com/world/all-about-germanys-hybrid-voting-system-and-the-key-5-threshold-ahead-of-feb-23-elections-13865714.html"],") – especially if population growth causes the number of general electorate seats to rise relative to the number of list seats."]},{"k":"p","s":["At the first MMP election, there were 65 electorate and 55 list seats; last week (and pre-overhang), there were 71 electorate seats and just 49 list seats."]},{"k":"p","s":["Unless that ratio is fixed – also recommended by the 2023 Independent Electoral Review – the number of electorate seats will keep increasing as the population grows."]},{"k":"p","s":["In such circumstances, a party with a strong electorate presence (National) could do well, especially if it were to align itself with other parties (ACT is the obvious choice here) that concentrate on the party vote."]},{"k":"p","s":["In this respect, National is in a much stronger position than Labour, whose electorate vote is more concentrated across fewer seats. Labour’s electorate vote is also shrinking as ",["Labour-leaning Māori voters shift onto the Māori roll","https://newsroom.co.nz/2026/11/08/the-real-reason-national-won-2-out-of-3-general-electorates-its-not-what-you-think/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Fixing the system"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are ways to ",["address the overhang problem","https://theconversation.com/what-really-drove-nzs-election-overhang-and-what-can-be-done-about-it-296144"],". Most obviously, the electoral law could be amended to either offset the consequences of overhangs or remove them entirely."]},{"k":"p","s":["Remedies might include abolishing the “coat-tail” provision that exempts parties from the 5% threshold for entering parliament if they win a single electorate seat, bringing in more candidates than their overall vote would otherwise allow."]},{"k":"p","s":["The party vote threshold could be lowered, and the ratio of electorate-to-list seats fixed at 50-50, as originally recommended by the 1986 ",["Royal Commission on the Electoral System","https://elections.nz/democracy-in-nz/what-is-new-zealands-system-of-government/report-of-the-royal-commission-on-the-electoral-system"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["National-led governments have passed up the opportunity to make these changes before. It seems unlikely a new one will break with precedent."]}],"chars":6081},"https://theconversation.com/ai-has-solved-a-host-of-big-maths-problems-heres-why-this-threatens-the-whole-field-of-mathematics-293982":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-23T18:37Z","sha":"bd16d5d1897134c7c46659b7f27d054c6670cf901cccaee655b917d760d58206","read":"https://theconversation.com/ai-has-solved-a-host-of-big-maths-problems-heres-why-this-threatens-the-whole-field-of-mathematics-293982","bytes":185119,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"AI has solved a host of big maths problems – here’s why this threatens the whole field of mathematics","by":[{"n":"Neil Saunders","r":"Senior Lecturer in Mathematics, Department of Mathematical Sciences, City St George's, University of London"}],"pub":"2026-11-23T12:27:56Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["For many, the year 2026 will be remembered as the one where mathematics had an identity crisis and forever changed. Frontier (cutting edge) AI models made by OpenAI and Anthropic made stunning progress on hundreds of open problems that have baffled mathematicians for decades – and centuries in some cases."]},{"k":"p","s":["From April this year, a steady stream of impressive AI-discovered results emerged. It started with a breakthrough by OpenAI on the Erdős ",["unit distance conjecture","https://theconversation.com/an-ai-solution-to-an-80-year-old-problem-has-shocked-mathematicians-283686"]," and the ",["Jacobian conjecture","https://theconversation.com/hello-there-the-jacobian-conjecture-is-false-thanx-why-a-tiny-social-media-post-has-mathematicians-rethinking-ai-283883"],", both of which had been unsolved for decades."]},{"k":"p","s":["Then, in September and October, two stunning announcements were made. First, Open AI announced a solution to the ",["Navier-Stokes problem","https://openai.com/index/navier-stokes-solution/"]," – one of the seven “millennium problems” highlighted by the ",["Clay Mathematics Institute","https://www.claymath.org/millennium-problems/"]," in the year 2000. Second, OpenAI released a ",["trove of over 700 papers","https://openai.com/index/sharing-ai-progress-in-mathematics/"]," claiming solutions, proofs or counter-examples (which show that a claim or conjecture is false) to 372 open problems that are at the forefront of mathematics research."]},{"k":"p","s":["Now, Anthropic researcher ",["Levent Alpöge","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Levent_Alp%C3%B6ge"]," has announced a ",["Claude-assisted proof","https://alpo.ge/remark.pdf"]," of the ",["Riemann Hypothesis","https://www.claymath.org/millennium/riemann-hypothesis/"],". This is arguably the most famous problem in mathematics, proposed by the German mathematician Bernhard Riemann in 1867."]},{"k":"p","s":["The October “Open AI dump” as it has become known, sent shock waves through the mathematics community because of its sheer scale. Hugo Duminil-Copin, professor and Fields medallist (the medal is a top accolade in mathematics), from the Institute of Advanced Scientific Studies in Paris, said the dump had ",["“annihilated my field of research”","https://www.lemonde.fr/en/science/article/2026/10/12/openai-s-latest-blow-to-mathematicians-they-have-annihilated-my-field-of-research_6758515_10.html"],". He also warned that it could “dismantle” the discipline of mathematics."]},{"k":"p","s":["How tech companies were able to make such staggering progress on difficult problems is that first, their specific AI technology, called large language models (LLMs), are trained on the entire human corpus of mathematical literature (and much more)."]},{"k":"p","s":["Second, the companies created “ ",["AI-agents","https://www.ibm.com/think/topics/ai-agents"],"”, software systems built around the LLM that extend its capabilities to reasoning, taking actions and executing code. Agents can also observe the results of their actions, taking further action if required."]},{"k":"p","s":["For the solution to the Navier-Stokes equation, OpenAI set ",["10,000 AI agents","https://openai.com/index/navier-stokes-solution/"]," to work collaboratively. It took 88 hours for these agents to find their solution. A further 17 hours was needed to have the solution verified through formalisation and verification software called ",["Lean","https://lean-lang.org/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Alpöge’s Claude-assisted proof of the Riemann Hypothesis runs to more than 250,000 pages. The Lean code verification is over ",["17 million lines long","https://www.quantamagazine.org/updates/transformation/"],". His Lean proof has since been ",["verified by independent researchers","https://www.scientificamerican.com/article/the-ai-riemann-hypothesis-proof-is-almost-certainly-true-independent-mathematicians-attest/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Unlike the ",["Poincaré Conjecture","https://www.claymath.org/millennium/poincare-conjecture/"],", a millennium problem solved by the Russian mathematician ",["Grigori Perelman","https://www.science.org/doi/10.1126/science.314.5807.1848"]," in the early 2000s, the Navier-Stokes equation, (like all the other 300 problems in the OpenAI dump), was resolved by AI agents with almost no human intervention."]},{"k":"p","s":["This is truly extraordinary. A metaphor illustrating how these agents work might be a colony of Australian ",["cathedral termites","https://meep.sydney.edu.au/how-cathedral-termites-arrived-to-build-their-skyscrapers/"],". Each insect in the colony mindlessly does its local thing but in concert, the termites build impressive castles, often over six metres high, replete with ventilation, a form of air conditioning and weather protection."]},{"k":"p","s":["Likewise, each AI agent chips away at its local task, but collectively, these swarms of agents can now solve – and verify – the hardest known maths problems."]},{"k":"h","s":["Mass production of results"]},{"k":"p","s":["All this has mathematicians worried. Terence Tao, professor of mathematics at the University of California, Los Angeles and a 2006 Fields medallist, recently suggested that the speed at which mathematical results are being AI-produced is actually ",["harming the discipline","https://www.newscientist.com/article/2588329-terence-tao-ai-companies-are-harming-mathematics/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Tao ",["likened","https://www.newscientist.com/article/2588329-terence-tao-ai-companies-are-harming-mathematics/"]," what AI companies are doing as “dumping carcasses of raw meat onto our table and saying ‘here you go, I solved your food problem’.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["On September 11, 2026, Tao and 25 other Fields medallists ",["produced a declaration","https://mathandai.org/"]," stating that “the goals of the AI companies and the goals of the mathematical community are severely misaligned”. The declaration warns that “the mass production at faster and faster pace of \"true/false” statements could destroy fertile ground instead of breathing life into new ideas\"."]},{"k":"p","s":["At the time of writing, this declaration has over 8,000 signatures from mathematicians globally. In a similar spirit, the recently formed ",["Association for Human Mathematics","https://www.ahmath.org/home"],", whose members “commit to conduct entirely AI-free research, centring human thinking and judgement in the mathematical sciences” has more than 1,000 members."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is an old idiom in AI ",["known as Moravec’s Paradox","https://epoch.ai/gradient-updates/moravec-s-paradox"],", which is often expressed as “hard problems are easy and the easy problems are hard”. This phrase explains why we have machines that are better at tasks humans find hard, such as chess, coding and now: mathematical research, but are worse at tasks that humans find easy, such as stacking the dishwasher without breaking plates."]},{"k":"p","s":["But mathematics is like chess and coding in some sense. It is a somewhat closed world of information that is ripe for AI to come in and extract patterns, find connections and perform calculations that allow it to generate results beyond human capability."]},{"k":"p","s":["So while fluency and proficiency in “hard” mathematical fields has traditionally been a benchmark of intelligence, both human and machine, these powerful multi-agent AI systems show that raw compute power, combined with an abundance of data, are sufficient to obtain results beyond the reach of many mathematicians over many lifetimes."]},{"k":"h","s":["A healthy ecosystem"]},{"k":"p","s":["However, an interesting footnote to this is that OpenAI estimated that the total cost of finding the solution to the Navier-Stokes equation was ",["US$15 million","https://www.newscientist.com/article/2588063-openai-has-solved-the-navier-stokes-millennium-problem-using-15m-of-ai-effort/"]," (£11.4 million) – thus a net loss of US$14 million if the Clay Institute were to award OpenAI the prize money."]},{"k":"p","s":["Thus, it is possible that the big tech companies will move on from mathematics if they do not see monetary value in continuing to prove open conjectures."]},{"k":"p","s":["By approaching a problem in a “bottom-up” way, mathematicians build theory and form connections between seemingly disparate sub-disciplines. They disseminate preliminary findings and partial results via journals, conference presentations and workshops."]},{"k":"p","s":["This engagement with the rest of the community includes PhD students and early career researchers, so that a new generation of mathematicians are being trained to take the field further."]},{"k":"p","s":["Many students of mathematics go on to fields where a strong mathematical training is invaluable, such as government, data science, education, sustainability, finance and cybersecurity. This ecosystem – essential for a flourishing society and economy – may be at risk if a new “top-down”, black-box, reverse engineered approach to mathematics becomes a new norm."]},{"k":"p","s":["So while having powerful AI tools to resolve longstanding problems presents new and exciting opportunities – indeed, I believe that there has ",["never been a better time","https://theconversation.com/ai-means-theres-no-better-time-to-study-maths-but-degrees-are-becoming-less-accessible-290111"]," to study maths – these have to be carefully balanced against the wider interests of the discipline as well as the wider interests of society."]}],"chars":7046},"https://theconversation.com/nvidias-ceo-is-back-but-the-turmoil-has-exposed-the-ai-booms-risks-for-nz-investors-296924":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-23T23:33Z","sha":"8052f6d1719102fb80e1915141a04bf4391c0e5181f59ce48934444a1bef6ef0","read":"https://theconversation.com/nvidias-ceo-is-back-but-the-turmoil-has-exposed-the-ai-booms-risks-for-nz-investors-296924","bytes":183620,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Nvidia’s CEO is back – but the turmoil has exposed the AI boom’s risks for NZ investors","by":[{"n":"Sara Ali","r":"Research Fellow and Academic Database Advisor, Department of Finance, Auckland University of Technology"}],"pub":"2026-11-23T22:01:55Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Jensen Huang ",["has returned to the helm","https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/nov/23/jensen-huang-reinstated-as-nvidia-chief-executive"]," of Nvidia. But ",["the extraordinary events","https://theconversation.com/why-is-nvidia-so-powerful-in-the-ai-world-and-what-could-jensen-huangs-scandal-really-cost-296257"]," surrounding the US chipmaker’s co-founder over the past two weeks have offered New Zealand investors a reminder of the risks of ",["the artificial intelligence (AI) boom","https://theconversation.com/feeling-unprepared-for-the-ai-boom-youre-not-alone-273192"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Huang ",["resigned","https://nvidianews.nvidia.com/news/nvidia-announces-ceo-transition"]," as chief executive on November 12 following revelations of extramarital affairs, including one with a Chinese businesswoman ",["reportedly suspected","https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/22/us/politics/alice-huang-china-spy-agency-nvidia.html"]," by US intelligence of espionage."]},{"k":"p","s":["Despite initially ruling out his return, Nvidia’s board ",["reinstated Huang","https://nvidianews.nvidia.com/news/nvidia-board-reinstates-jensen-huang-as-president-ceo-and-board-director"]," on November 23, saying it was satisfied he posed no national security risk. The decision ",["reportedly followed lobbying","https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/23/us/politics/trump-nvidia-huang.html"]," from US President Donald Trump."]},{"k":"p","s":["The turmoil sent Nvidia’s shares on a rollercoaster ride. Between their October peak and mid-November, ",["nearly NZ$1.3 billion was wiped","https://www.nzherald.co.nz/business/nvidia-crash-new-zealand-superannuation-fund-takes-13b-hit/Z6DET2C5YJA4JGUQ65A6TLHHVI/"]," from the value of the New Zealand Superannuation Fund’s Nvidia holdings, as the chipmaker’s share price fell about 30%."]},{"k":"p","s":["Nvidia’s underlying business remains strong. In its ",["latest earnings report","https://nvidianews.nvidia.com/news/nvidia-announces-financial-results-for-third-quarter-fiscal-2027"],", the company reported quarterly revenue of US$115.8 billion, more than double the same period last year."]},{"k":"p","s":["But the episode illustrates how uncertainty surrounding one of the world’s biggest tech companies can affect New Zealanders’ retirement savings – including KiwiSaver members who ",["may have little idea","https://theconversation.com/when-ai-giants-go-public-will-ordinary-investors-know-if-they-are-along-for-the-ride-282963"]," how much of their money is invested in tech giants."]},{"k":"h","s":["How exposed are our savings to big tech?"]},{"k":"p","s":["At ",["its last full disclosure","https://nzsuperfund.nz/publications/disclosures/annual-equity-listings/"]," in June, the Super Fund’s five largest overseas shareholdings were Nvidia, Apple, Microsoft, Amazon and Google’s owner, Alphabet. Together, they were worth about NZ$10.6 billion – about one dollar in every five the fund holds directly in overseas shares."]},{"k":"p","s":["But this isn’t necessarily a deliberate bet on tech. A handful of US tech companies ",["make up about one third","https://www.fool.com/research/magnificent-seven-sp-500/?facet=app&mode=dark"]," of the benchmark US sharemarket index, the S&P 500. Funds investing broadly in world markets therefore hold large positions in these companies."]},{"k":"p","s":["KiwiSaver funds have similar exposure. As of September 30, Nvidia accounted for about 5.5% of investments in ",["Kernel’s High Growth fund","https://www.smartinvestor.sorted.org.nz/disclose-document/23834652bf3e59cd/High-Growth-FU-KS----Kiwi-Saver-Update---Sept-2026.pdf"]," and ",["Generate’s Focused Growth fund","https://www.smartinvestor.sorted.org.nz/disclose-document/cd603231a5b70638/FU-2026-Q-3-KS-Focused-Growth.pdf"],", and 5.2% in ",["Simplicity’s High Growth fund","https://www.smartinvestor.sorted.org.nz/disclose-document/638c8701756037be/Simplicity-High-Growth-Fund-update-30-September-2026.pdf"],". By comparison, it made up less than 2% of ",["Fisher Funds’ KiwiSaver Plan Growth fund","https://www.smartinvestor.sorted.org.nz/disclose-document/b4f78a676c9cdeb1/Fisher-Funds-Kiwi-Saver-Plan-Growth-Fund-30-September-2026--Fund-Update.pdf"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["For someone with $50,000 in either of the first two funds, that meant about $2,750 was tied to Nvidia shares alone. While investing in several big technology companies might spread the risk, some vulnerabilities are easy to overlook."]},{"k":"p","s":["One concerns leadership. In less than two weeks, Nvidia’s founder resigned, the board ruled out his return, and then reinstated him. Each development brought new uncertainty for investors, showing how quickly events involving a single executive can affect a company’s fortunes."]},{"k":"p","s":["Another is how closely these companies depend on each other. Anthropic, the ",["freshly floated","https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2026/nov/19/anthropic-float-stock-market-nasdaq-raises-81bn-record-ipo-latest-news-updates"]," AI company behind Claude, ",["has committed to spending","https://www.statista.com/chart/36744/anthropics-compute-and-infrastructure-commitments/"]," more than US$250 billion on computing capacity from Google, Amazon and Microsoft."]},{"k":"p","s":["Three of the Super Fund’s five largest holdings are partly dependent on the same customer. When AI spending rises, their fortunes may rise together. If it slows, they could fall together."]},{"k":"p","s":["Nvidia ",["has guaranteed up to US$118 billion","https://www.techtarget.com/news/nvidia-backs-ai-infrastructure-buildout-with-118b-in-guarantees/875051/"]," of its partners’ data centre costs, including ",["US$105 billion for an Ohio campus","https://www.reuters.com/business/media-telecom/nvidia-invest-15-billion-sb-energy-under-openai-data-center-deal-2026-08-17/"]," leased to OpenAI. It has made no payments so far, but these guarantees tie its fortunes more closely to its customers."]},{"k":"p","s":["A further risk lies in government policy. On November 16, the US Commerce Department ",["issued a rule","https://www.nbcnews.com/tech/tech-news/us-closes-loophole-let-chinese-companies-use-top-ai-chips-rcna609634"]," requiring licences to export advanced AI chips to five countries, while limiting remote access to US chips through overseas data centres."]},{"k":"p","s":["Decisions made in Washington can quickly change the earnings outlook for these companies."]},{"k":"h","s":["Why some funds are more exposed than others"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Index funds","https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/investing-basics/investment-products/mutual-funds-and-exchange-traded-4"],", often called passive funds, track a market index. They hold companies in proportion to their size, so as tech companies rise in value, their weight increases. Exposure also depends on which index they follow."]},{"k":"p","s":["As of September 30, the index-based high growth funds from Kernel and Simplicity had more of their overseas shares in Nvidia, Apple and Microsoft than the main global share index, ",["MSCI’s All Country World Index","https://www.msci.com/indexes/index/892400/msci-acwi-index"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Active managers can hold more or less than that index. Generate leaned into Nvidia and Microsoft. Milford’s growth funds held about twice the index’s share of Microsoft, with Apple at or below it. Fisher Funds held less than the index in all three."]},{"k":"p","s":["Neither approach is automatically safer. ",["Research","https://www.morningstar.com.au/insights/personal-finance/BCHJM6XIBBEDTLUQ3HV3EE4DPI/young-invested-why-these-etfs-keep-winning"]," by investment analysis firm Morningstar on funds sold in Australia found many actively managed global share funds performed worse than index funds while big tech shares were rising – partly because they held less of them."]},{"k":"p","s":["But when those shares fall, as Nvidia’s did earlier this month, the funds holding the most feel it first."]},{"k":"h","s":["What can KiwiSaver members do?"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Super Fund is built to ride out falls over decades. Many KiwiSaver members have less time, especially those close to 65 or saving for a first home."]},{"k":"p","s":["One step is to check a fund’s largest holdings. Every KiwiSaver fund publishes its ten largest investments each quarter, available on Sorted’s ",["Smart Investor website","https://www.smartinvestor.sorted.org.nz/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Another is to consider whether the fund type matches the investment timeline. High growth funds generally suit money that won’t be needed for at least ten years. For shorter timeframes, a more balanced fund may be appropriate."]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s important to avoid selling in a panic. Switching to a conservative fund after a market fall can lock in losses and mean missing a recovery."]},{"k":"p","s":["The AI boom may continue. But Nvidia’s turmoil shows how, when so much of New Zealanders’ savings is concentrated in a few companies, their troubles can quickly become ours."]}],"chars":5688}};
